  "description": "EQEDAI crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C145 H155 Br10 Cd6 Eu4 N15 O50 4+,4(N1 O3 1-),C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd3 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd4 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Cd5 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd6 (Cd) has 3 O neighbors; Cd7? (Cd) has 0 O neighbors; Cd8? (Cd) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.647-4.285 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.13-111.38°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C146H157Br10Cd6Cl2Eu4N19O62. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
